From: Timepiece Project
Subject: [PATCH] Verso: emit fragment anchors for empty-path ToC entries

`Toc.html` renders each table-of-contents entry as a link. When a part has
no path of its own (`path.isEmpty`), it emitted `href="/"`. In the
single-page HTML output (`emitHtmlSingle`), every top-level part has an empty
path, so the entire in-body "Table of Contents" rendered as `href="/"` (which
the browser relativizes to `href=""` against `<base href="./">`). Clicking any
of those entries navigated to the output *directory* — showing a file listing
— instead of scrolling to the section, forcing the reader to click
`index.html` by hand.

For an empty path, the correct link is a pure fragment anchor `#<htmlId>`,
which resolves to the current document and scrolls to the section. Use the
part's `id` (an `Option String`) to build it, falling back to `"/"` only when
no id is present (preserving the old behaviour for that edge case). Non-empty
paths still use `path.link id`, so multi-page output is unaffected.

Applies to verso v4.28.0 (commit 372f82ee4e67c863cf473a9174a1a77e0bec74a2).

--- a/src/verso-manual/VersoManual/Html.lean
+++ b/src/verso-manual/VersoManual/Html.lean
@@ -213,7 +213,10 @@ public partial def Toc.html (depth : Option Nat) : Toc → Html
   | {title, shortTitle := _, path, id, sectionNum, children} =>
     if depth = some 0 then .empty
     else
       let page :=
-        if path.isEmpty then "/"
+        -- An empty path means the part has no page of its own (single-page output).
+        -- Link to its fragment anchor so the entry scrolls in place instead of
+        -- navigating to the output directory (which shows a file listing).
+        if path.isEmpty then id.map (fun htmlId => "#" ++ htmlId) |>.getD "/"
         else path.link id
       let sectionNum :=
         match sectionNum with
